    guide: 'The month so far, for the owner, from Crest IMS and Crest HR together. It opens with one sentence: how much of every NPR 100 you sell the business keeps (Net Margin), then what to look at. Below it: Revenue so far, Spend % so far (stock bought divided by sales: the month has not been counted yet, so it cannot be Food Cost %), Labor Cost %, Prime Cost % (Spend % so far plus Labor Cost %) and Net Margin % (Revenue less stock bought, labour, overheads, tax and fees, and what delivery partners such as Foodmandu and Pathao kept from bills sold this month). A Needs you list follows (items below par, supplier bills over 60 days unpaid), then Wastage, Purchases by cash and credit, and a Cost and Margin trend over your last 12 closed months, each point read from that month frozen Owner Report. Ratios count the days already finished, and rent and other fixed costs are counted for those days only, so the margin is the real rate of the month. Revenue is before VAT. Stock bought adds stock received from your other outlets and takes off stock sent to them. Tap Net Margin to open this month on Profit & Loss, which sets the same figure out line by line. Requires both Crest IMS and Crest HR, plus Crest Suite Pro, an add-on bought on top of your modules and switched on from the Billing tab in Manage Clients.',
