    icon: 'Σ', name: 'Profit & Loss (Consolidated P&L)', featureKey: 'consolidated_pnl',
    guide: 'The formal statement the dashboards are not: Revenue, Cost of Goods Sold (food used), Gross Profit, then Wastage, Staff Meals, Delivery commission, Labour, Overheads and Tax & Fees down to Net Profit, each line with its share of revenue — for one BS month, or pick a fiscal year to see Shrawan to Ashadh added up. Every figure comes from the module that owns it: revenue and COGS use the same rules as Monthly Summary (price actually charged, comps excluded, sub-recipes counted at their raw ingredients), Labour, on an outlet that runs Crest HR, is your finalized Payroll run (pay earned — salary less unpaid days and days before joining — plus overtime plus employer SSF, the payroll sheet\'s Cost to business), plus any festival allowance, incentives and leavers\' final settlements finalized for that month; until it is finalized, the HR estimate from the staff list, marked as an estimate, and a Labor tab entry is then shown as not counted. Without Crest HR, labour is the Labour bucket from Overheads. Never both. Delivery commission (Foodmandu, Pathao) is its own line, counted in the month the bill was sold, from what you recorded when the partner paid. Depreciation from posted Fixed Asset runs is shown under Net Profit as a memo, the way Overheads shows it, and is not subtracted: Net Profit is before depreciation, interest and income tax. Defaults to your most recent closed month, because COGS needs the closing stock count; an open month\'s profit is shown without a colour until it is closed. If your outlets are linked into a group, the same page shows one column per outlet plus a consolidated total — only outlets whose own Crest Suite Pro is live are included (an outlet whose Suite has ended drops out after the 7-day grace, as its own pages do), and the ones left out are named. Stock moved between your outlets cancels out in the consolidated column, and stock still on the way at a month\'s end is named under the statement. Part of Crest Suite Pro.',
